s(1).v = 4;
s(2).v = 6;
s(3).v = 1;
disp(sum([s.v]) * numel(s))
```

What does the first `fprintf` print? (`%g` prints a number in its shortest natural form, followed here by a space.)

```matlab
x = str2double({'3.5', 'n/a', '1e2', ' 7 '});
fprintf('%g ', x);
fprintf('\n');
```

What does this Octave script print?

```matlab
1;
function bumpMap(m)
  m('n') = m('n') + 1;
end
function bumpStruct(s)
  s.n = s.n + 1;
end

m = containers.Map();
m('n') = 1;
s.n = 1;
bumpMap(m);
bumpStruct(s);
fprintf('%d %d\n', m('n'), s.n);
```

What does this print?

```matlab
[u, ~, k] = unique({'oak', 'ash', 'oak', 'elm', 'oak', 'ash'});
counts = accumarray(k(:), 1)';
fprintf('%s:%d ', u{1}, counts(1), u{end}, counts(end));
fprintf('\n');
```
